[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2607231100-kawaraban-kotoba-wasm-cacao-aozora-phase-b", :adr/title "ADR-2607231100: kawaraban kotoba-wasm componentization Phase B — CACAO self-mint + aozora XRPC confined slices", :adr/status "accepted", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2607231100: kawaraban kotoba-wasm componentization Phase B\n\n**Status**: accepted (実装-layer, execution-substrate change only — NOT a charter amendment)\n**Date**: 2026-07-23\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\ncom-junkawasaki/root's ADR-2607110200 (kawaraban R0→R1) already established kawaraban's\nCACAO self-mint (`src/kawaraban/cacao.clj`) and aozora publish path\n(`src/kawaraban/aozora.clj`) as JVM Clojure, 1:1 ports of tashikame's proven shape. This\nrepo's own CLAUDE.md already frames kawaraban's one-sentence identity as \"a news MEDIUM,\n**kotoba-wasm-native**, on the Murakumo fleet\" — this ADR is the first concrete step\ntoward that stated identity, not a new direction.\n\ncom-junkawasaki/root ADR-2607231022 (\"Phase A\", `kotoba-lang/kototama` PR #49) registered\nfour new `actor:host` ABI capabilities kawaraban needs to run as a `.kotoba` guest:\n`http-fetch` (GET-only), `cbor-encode`, `json-encode`, `json-extract-field` — alongside the\nalready-available `identity/keypair`, `identity/sign`, `hash/sha256`, `http/post`.\n\n## Decision\n\n**Port a confined slice of `cacao.clj`/`aozora.clj` to `.kotoba`, compiled via `kotoba wasm\nemit` and hosted via `kotoba-lang/kototama`'s `kototama.tender` (real Chicory JVM\nexecution) — NOT the RSS/Atom fetch+parse or the G1–G11 charter gates.**\n\nThree new modules land in `com-etzhayyim-kawaraban`'s `wasm/` (see that repo's\n`wasm/README.md` for full ABI/design/gap detail):\n\n- `cacao_self_mint.kotoba` — fresh Ed25519 identity (`identity/keypair`) + SHA-256\n  fingerprint of the pubkey (`hash/sha256`) + Ed25519 signature over a host-formatted SIWE\n  message (`identity/sign`) + flat CBOR encode (`data/cbor`). Verified: the guest-generated\n  pubkey's fingerprint matches an independently computed SHA-256, and the guest's signature\n  genuinely verifies against that pubkey/message via `ed25519.core/verify` — real\n  cryptography, not a stub.\n- `aozora_create_session.kotoba` — builds `com.atproto.server.createSession`'s real\n  `{\"cacao\": \"...\"}` JSON envelope (`data/json`) and POSTs it (`http/post`) to a loopback\n  target ON PURPOSE (no live internet access this session) — proves real compiler+tender\n  linkage and real SSRF-guard execution, the same proof shape kototama's own\n  `kotoba-compiled-http-fetch.kotoba` fixture already established.\n- `aozora_extract_session_fields.kotoba` — pulls `accessJwt` out of an example\n  createSession response (`data/json`).\n\n**RSS/Atom fetch+parse (`methods/live_fetch.cljc`) stays JVM-side, unchanged.** `.kotoba`\ngenuinely cannot express it: no runtime string search/slice, no unbounded loop over\nnetwork-response-length input, no XML/tag-matching facility — confirmed empirically (not\nassumed) by reading `kotoba-lang/kotoba`'s actual WASM code-generator, and independently\nconfirmed by three prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` wasm ports reaching the identical\nconclusion by the same method. `methods/ingest.cljc`'s G1/G3/G4 charter-gate logic is\nequally untouched.\n\n**This is not a byte-faithful production port.** Concrete, documented gaps (see\n`wasm/README.md` \"Language-limitation findings\"): `cbor-encode`/`json-encode` only produce\na FLAT single-level map (the real CACAO wire is nested `{\"h\":{...},\"p\":{...},\"s\":{...}}`,\nso this module's CBOR output is a flat approximation, not wire-compatible with a real\nCACAO-verifying server); `http-post` has no header parameter (blocks\n`com.atproto.repo.createRecord`'s required `Authorization: Bearer` — not attempted here);\ndid:key / graph-cid derivation needs bignum encoding this language cannot express and\nstays host-side. None of these are silently papered over.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- kawaraban's CACAO self-mint and the aozora `createSession` HTTP-envelope-building /\n  response-field-extraction steps now have working, tested, capability-sandboxed WASM\n  equivalents — real Chicory-hosted execution proven via `test/wasm/*_test.clj`\n  (`clojure -M:test` — 29 tests / 56 assertions, 0 failures/errors).\n- The G1–G11 charter gates are unweakened and untouched — this ADR changes execution\n  substrate for the CACAO/XRPC boundary only, never the charter or the article-content\n  path.\n- Fleet placement on Murakumo (a later Phase D) and the follow-up capability extensions\n  (nested CBOR maps, HTTP headers, did:key bignum encoding) are explicitly deferred, not\n  silently dropped — see `wasm/README.md`'s Follow-ups section.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **Port RSS/Atom parsing to `.kotoba` too** — rejected. The language subset cannot express\n  it (confirmed by direct inspection of the compiler, not merely presumed); forcing it\n  would mean either a hidden host-side fallback disguised as a wasm port, or an unsafe\n  ad-hoc parser inside the sandbox that the language's own admission gates would reject\n  outright for most real-world feed shapes.\n- **Produce a byte-faithful nested CACAO CBOR token from `.kotoba` now** — rejected for this\n  pass. Requires a capability-surface extension to `kototama`/`kotoba-core-contracts`\n  (nested-map CBOR encode) that is a legitimate, separate Phase C decision, not something\n  to bolt on unilaterally inside a single actor's port.\n\n## References\n\n- com-junkawasaki/root ADR-2607110200 (kawaraban R0→R1 design, JVM Clojure `cacao.clj`/\n  `aozora.clj`).\n- com-junkawasaki/root ADR-2607231022 (\"Phase A\" — kototama `actor:host` ABI second wave:\n  `http-fetch`/`cbor-encode`/`json-encode`/`json-extract-field`).\n- `kotoba-lang/kototama` PR #49, `kotoba-lang/kotoba-core-contracts` PR #10.\n- `com-etzhayyim-kawaraban`'s own `wasm/README.md` (full design, ABI, gap list, rebuild\n  instructions) — the detailed technical record this pointer ADR summarizes.\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2607231100-kawaraban-kotoba-wasm-cacao-aozora-phase-b.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "kawaraban-kotoba-wasm-componentization", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-23", :adr/date "2026-07-23", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["com-etzhayyim-kawaraban/wasm/README.md" "com-etzhayyim-kawaraban/wasm/cacao_self_mint.kotoba" "com-etzhayyim-kawaraban/wasm/aozora_create_session.kotoba" "com-etzhayyim-kawaraban/wasm/aozora_extract_session_fields.kotoba" "90-docs/adr/2606061900-kawaraban-news-medium-actor-r0.edn" "com-junkawasaki/root:90-docs/adr/2607110200-kawaraban-r0-r1-cloud-itonami-isco-3521-media-broadcast.edn" "com-junkawasaki/root:90-docs/adr/2607231022-kototama-http-fetch-cbor-json-capabilities.edn" "kotoba-lang/kototama#49" "kotoba-lang/kotoba-core-contracts#10"], :adr/authoritative_for ["kawaraban's kotoba-wasm componentization scope decision: CACAO self-mint + aozora createSession JSON/POST/field-extraction are ported to real .kotoba/WASM modules; RSS/Atom fetch+parse and the G1-G11 charter gates are NOT ported and stay JVM-side" "the honest gap list for this port (flat-only CBOR/JSON encode, no HTTP headers, no did:key/graph-cid bignum encoding, no live internet calls made) as of 2026-07-23 -- not a claim of a byte-faithful production port"]}]
